<title>CHILE: Chile Sept-Nov unemployment falls to 5.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Chile Sept-Nov unemployment falls to 5.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's unemployment rate fell to 5.9 percent in the September-November quarter, down 0.3 percent from the August-October period and down 0.9 percent from the September-November quarter of 1995, the National Statistics Institute said.</p>
<p>The workforce totalled 5.54 million people in the September-November period, up 0.5 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>Government figures showed 76,000 new jobs have been created over the last year, said the institute.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago Newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
